From 29eb11627afb1f9cbb4e364d6ddbf9c2c79075fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:19:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVBridge: "As SDR" and the choices of an HLG video in the
 output of a video

The output chosen for the video that plays (the list of the video settings
of the player, the button of the video OSD and of the player information,
PlayerControl(HadesDVOutput)) offered native Dolby Vision, Dolby Vision as
HDR10 or HDR10+, measured, or Kodi's own output, for Dolby Vision, HDR10 and
HDR10+ videos, and only where the display takes Dolby Vision for the last
two. A display whose HDR looks worse than its SDR (a projector, a TV with a
poor HDR mode) could have HLG, HDR10 and HDR10+ sent as SDR only for every
video at once ("Play HDR videos as SDR"), and Dolby Vision never; an HLG
video had no choice at all: HLG as Dolby Vision was the setting's alone.

- A new choice, "As SDR (without HDR)" (OutputChoice::SDR), for any HDR
  video on an output that would send its HDR (Kodi's HDR output is on and
  the display takes HDR): never native, no HDR signalling, the picture
  mapped to SDR as on a display without HDR, by the tone mapping method of
  the video (the bridge's mapping with Reference (BT.2390), the default,
  Kodi's with its own). Dolby Vision is rebuilt and mapped where it is so on
  a display without HDR (profile 5 always, 7 and 8.1 with the reference
  method); elsewhere its base layer goes out as SDR. Profile 5 is offered it
  only where it can be rebuilt (OpenGL ES 3, nothing failed).
- The pictures of a stream opened for that choice say so
  (VideoPicture::hdrAsSdrChosen, set by the decoder when it opens, as
  doviNoNative is), so that the pictures decoded before a change keep the
  output they had: the renderer, SetHDR() and the bridge take the choice
  from the picture, the mode change and the decoder from the choice.
- An HLG video has the list too: as the settings say, "HLG as Dolby
  Vision" (wherever native output is had, whatever the setting says, as an
  HDR10+ video's "Dolby Vision made from its HDR10+ metadata" does), as
  Kodi plays it (HLG), and as SDR. An HLG stream made Dolby Vision follows
  the choice through CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::DVOutputChoiceChanged(), as HDR10
  measured does.
- For an HDR10, HDR10+ or HLG video, Kodi's own output is listed only where
  the display takes Dolby Vision (elsewhere it is what "As the settings
  say" gives). The list of a video that does not play as Dolby Vision is
  called "HDR output (this video)", and so is the help of the OSD button.
- The choice is kept for the file (DVOutputMemory: 8, which 1.0 leaves out
  when it reads it) and holds where the output would still send HDR.
- kodi.log says which picture went out as SDR by the choice, and the
  decoder's line of a Dolby Vision stream says it was decoded for it.

The idea of SDR in the list of a video's output is YBLOD's (its kodi-9962)
and CroqueMr's (Quick Switch); HLG in it is CroqueMr's.

Strings: core #41940-#41942 in English, translated in Estuary (#33940-

Tested on the host: the rules of DVPlaybackPolicy.h and DVOutputMemory.h
(the sources, what is offered and kept, what Dolby Vision is rebuilt for,
HLG as Dolby Vision chosen), eleven mutants each caught, and a sweep of
every function the change touches over the inputs that existed before it,
which prints the same with the header of the base (27416 lines). Compiled
with the build's commands. Not seen on a display.
